{
  "sn36.19:0.1": "Linked Discourses 36.19 ",
  "sn36.19:0.2": "2. In Private ",
  "sn36.19:0.3": "With Pañcakaṅga ",
  "sn36.19:1.1": "Then the chamberlain Pañcakaṅga went up to Venerable Udāyī, bowed, sat down to one side, and asked him, ",
  "sn36.19:1.2": "“Sir, how many feelings has the Buddha spoken of?” ",
  "sn36.19:1.3": "“Chamberlain, the Buddha has spoken of three feelings: ",
  "sn36.19:1.4": "pleasant, painful, and neutral. ",
  "sn36.19:1.5": "The Buddha has spoken of these three feelings.” ",
  "sn36.19:1.6": "When he said this, Pañcakaṅga said to Udāyī, ",
  "sn36.19:1.7": "“Sir, Udāyī, the Buddha hasn’t spoken of three feelings. ",
  "sn36.19:1.8": "He’s spoken of two feelings: ",
  "sn36.19:1.9": "pleasant and painful. ",
  "sn36.19:1.10": "The Buddha said that neutral feeling is included as a peaceful and subtle kind of pleasure.” ",
  "sn36.19:2.1": "For a second time, Udāyī said to him, ",
  "sn36.19:2.2": "“The Buddha hasn’t spoken of two feelings, ",
  "sn36.19:2.3": "he’s spoken of three.” ",
  "sn36.19:2.4": "",
  "sn36.19:2.5": "",
  "sn36.19:2.6": "For a second time, Pañcakaṅga said to Udāyī, ",
  "sn36.19:2.7": "“The Buddha hasn’t spoken of three feelings, ",
  "sn36.19:2.8": "he’s spoken of two.” ",
  "sn36.19:2.9": "",
  "sn36.19:2.10": "",
  "sn36.19:3.1": "And for a third time, Udāyī said to him, ",
  "sn36.19:3.2": "“The Buddha hasn’t spoken of two feelings, ",
  "sn36.19:3.3": "he’s spoken of three.” ",
  "sn36.19